# Copy to `.env.local` (which is gitignored) and adjust if you need to.
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser bundle. That
# prefix is a deliberate safety rail in Vite: it makes it impossible to leak a
# server secret into client-side JavaScript by accident, because a variable
# without the prefix simply is not substituted. Never put a secret in here —
# everything in this file ends up readable in the shipped bundle.

# Origin of the SeatLock API, WITHOUT the /api/v1 path (the client appends it).
#
# Leave it EMPTY for local development. An empty value makes the app request
# same-origin paths like /api/v1/events, which Vite's dev proxy (see
# vite.config.ts) forwards to Spring Boot on http://localhost:8080. Keeping dev
# same-origin means no CORS preflights locally, so the browser behaves the same
# way it will in production behind nginx.
#
# Set it only when the API lives on a different host from the static files, e.g.
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.seatlock.example
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
